 "title": "Oracle linework for u2 centre 300x300 (crop offset y240 x711). Hand waypoints in crop pixel coordinates (x right, y down).",
 "how_made": "Waypoints were read by eye from 6x enlarged tiles of the crop with a 10 px grid. Code snaps each waypoint to the lowest-cost pixel within snap_r and joins them with a minimum-cost 8-connected path on a label-free contrast map (dE to a 15x15 median). Checked only with --preview overlays (traces drawn on the image), never with any metric. G1-G3 (faint pale-orange straight lines, contrast ~25 dE) are given as fixed straight traces at the row of minimum brightness measured from row means over x 60-92 (G1 rows 59-61 -> centre 60, G2 156, G3 253): in the first preview the cost path for them jumped toward the much stronger red faults at crossings.",
